# ===========================================================================
# THIS IS THE ONLY FILE YOU FILL IN.
#
# bootstrap.sh creates config/agents.env from this template (0600,
# gitignored) and then waits while you edit it. Everything the build needs
# from you is here. Your coding agent can help -- it is a normal file.
#
# Defaults are fine for a first build. The only thing worth stopping for is
# Telegram, and you can leave that blank and add it later.
#
# Never commit the filled-in copy, and never paste these values into a chat
# with an agent -- that puts them in a transcript you do not control.
# Installed into the guest at ~/.config/agent-sandbox/agents.env and read by
# the agent services through a systemd EnvironmentFile.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Identity ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Just names. An agent's character lives in its own SOUL.md inside the VM --
# you change that by talking to the agent ("show me your SOUL.md", "add this
# paragraph"), not by editing anything here. See docs/personality.md.
OPENCLAW_AGENT_NAME="claw-one"
HERMES_AGENT_NAME="hermes-one"

# --- Gateway auth -----------------------------------------------------------
# Blank here on purpose, and NOT a shared secret: this template is committed
# to a public repo, so a value sitting in it would be the same for everyone
# who ever cloned it. Yours is generated fresh, per install.
#
# In your copy (config/agents.env, gitignored) bootstrap.sh has already put
# 64 random hex characters here. Nothing to do -- skip this field.
#
# Writing this file by hand instead? Generate the value, do not invent one:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#
# It authenticates CLI calls to the OpenClaw gateway inside the VM. The
# gateway binds loopback only and the VM has no port forwards, so this is
# defence in depth rather than a perimeter.
OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN=""

# --- Telegram ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Dedicated bot per agent from @BotFather -- never a personal account.
# Leave blank to build without channels; they stay disabled until verification
# passes either way. See spec/pi-target-state.md.
OPENCLAW_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=""
HERMES_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=""
# Your numeric Telegram user id -- the only account allowed to talk to the bots.
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_ID=""

# --- Local fallback model (DGX Spark, over Tailscale) ------------------------
# Leave blank to skip failover entirely.
# UNVERIFIED: the tailnet was unreachable when this repo was built, and the
# failover syntax for each agent is unconfirmed. See docs/failover.md.
VLLM_BASE_URL=""
VLLM_API_KEY=""
VLLM_MODEL=""
